# Add patterns of files dvc should ignore, which could improve
# the performance. Learn more at
# https://dvc.org/doc/user-guide/dvcignore

# Python bytecode caches.
#
# Datasets that embed this workflow as a submodule typically declare
# `modules/mkobj/workflow` as a DVC dependency. Running the workflow writes .pyc
# files into workflow/scripts/__pycache__/, and bytecode is not reproducible —
# its size and contents depend on the interpreter version and on source mtimes —
# so the dependency can never hash equal twice. The stage then reports
# "changed deps" on every `dvc repro`, which for an expensive stage means either
# re-running it or freezing it to work around the drift.
#
# Ignoring these loses nothing: .pyc files are derived from .py files that are
# themselves tracked.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
